{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M7eykYMTSLtot5Ybtjx7xv","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"select-tests: [tests].select for attavo build/verify/test (issue #103,\nmade fail-safe by issue #212).\n\nReads changed paths on stdin, one per line, and prints test identifiers\non stdout, one per line, for this repository's own test suite:\n\n  - prose (*.md, LICENSE) and this repository's own specs and records\n    (attest/specs/**, attest/records/**) select nothing;\n  - a test file (tests/test_*.py) selects itself, and the whole suite\n    when it no longer exists -- a deletion cannot select itself, and the\n    fail-safe rule below applies to it rather than exempting it (issue\n    #212's review);\n  - a module of attavo/ selects the tests written for it (MODULE_TESTS)\n    together with every test file that imports it, directly or through\n    other modules of attavo/ (a static import graph built from the source\n    with ast; nothing is imported or run), so a module most of the others\n    import (common, records, spec, ...) selects the test files that reach\n    it by import and not the whole suite (#317). A test that only runs\n    bin/attavo in a subprocess does not import anything and is not reached\n    by the graph: CI's full suite is the law, and it catches that miss\n    before merge;\n  - a prefix in PREFIX_TESTS (adapters/, schema/, templates/,\n    .github/workflows/, adapters/fixture/) and a few single files\n    (bin/attavo, action.yml, ...) select the tests that name them;\n  - a path this selector cannot place -- a module no table and no import\n    reaches, scripts/, a fixture every test stands on -- selects the whole\n    suite (\"tests\", the one path pytest needs to run everything), one such\n    path is enough to make that the whole answer, and the reason is\n    printed on stderr, one line per such path.\n\nUsage: <changed paths> | select-tests\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ast\nimport functools\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nWHOLE_SUITE = \"tests\"\n\nSILENT_PREFIXES = (\"attest/specs/\", \"attest/records/\")\n\nMODULE_TESTS: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\n    \"attavo/attest.py\": (\"tests/test_attest.py\", \"tests/test_attest_time.py\"),\n    \"attavo/build.py\": (\"tests/test_build.py\", \"tests/test_testtool.py\"),\n    \"attavo/claims.py\": (\"tests/test_claims.py\",),\n    \"attavo/clock.py\": (\"tests/test_clock.py\", \"tests/test_retry.py\"),\n    \"attavo/cli.py\": (\"tests/test_cli_help.py\", \"tests/test_testtool.py\"),\n    \"attavo/counsel.py\": (\"tests/test_counsel.py\",),\n    \"attavo/doctor.py\": (\"tests/test_doctor.py\", \"tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\",\n                         \"tests/test_proof_five_elsewhere.py\",\n                         \"tests/test_sealed_since_default.py\"),\n    \"attavo/drive.py\": (\"tests/test_drive.py\",),\n    \"attavo/workcopy.py\": (\"tests/test_working_copy.py\",),\n    \"attavo/filing.py\": (\"tests/test_file_findings.py\", \"tests/test_file_stops.py\"),\n    \"attavo/frontier.py\": (\"tests/test_frontier.py\",),\n    \"attavo/issues.py\": (\"tests/test_issues.py\", \"tests/test_frontier.py\"),\n    \"attavo/ledger.py\": (\"tests/test_ledger.py\",),","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c3f1140-993e-4968-9210-44f00ce30b29","uuid":"9294c467-8577-4653-8a51-523197eb3d1c","timestamp":"2026-10-15T20:08:31.907Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"select-tests: [tests].select for attavo build/verify/test (issue #103,\nmade fail-safe by issue #212).\n\nReads changed paths on stdin, one per line, and prints test identifiers\non stdout, one per line, for this repository's own test suite:\n\n  - prose (*.md, LICENSE) and this repository's own specs and records\n    (attest/specs/**, attest/records/**) select nothing;\n  - a test file (tests/test_*.py) selects itself, and the whole suite\n    when it no longer exists -- a deletion cannot select itself, and the\n    fail-safe rule below applies to it rather than exempting it (issue\n    #212's review);\n  - a module of attavo/ selects the tests written for it (MODULE_TESTS)\n    together with every test file that imports it, directly or through\n    other modules of attavo/ (a static import graph built from the source\n    with ast; nothing is imported or run), so a module most of the others\n    import (common, records, spec, ...) selects the test files that reach\n    it by import and not the whole suite (#317). A test that only runs\n    bin/attavo in a subprocess does not import anything and is not reached\n    by the graph: CI's full suite is the law, and it catches that miss\n    before merge;\n  - a prefix in PREFIX_TESTS (adapters/, schema/, templates/,\n    .github/workflows/, adapters/fixture/) and a few single files\n    (bin/attavo, action.yml, ...) select the tests that name them;\n  - a path this selector cannot place -- a module no table and no import\n    reaches, scripts/, a fixture every test stands on -- selects the whole\n    suite (\"tests\", the one path pytest needs to run everything), one such\n    path is enough to make that the whole answer, and the reason is\n    printed on stderr, one line per such path.\n\nUsage: <changed paths> | select-tests\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ast\nimport functools\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nWHOLE_SUITE = \"tests\"\n\nSILENT_PREFIXES = (\"attest/specs/\", \"attest/records/\")\n\nMODULE_TESTS: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\n    \"attavo/attest.py\": (\"tests/test_attest.py\", \"tests/test_attest_time.py\"),\n    \"attavo/build.py\": (\"tests/test_build.py\", \"tests/test_testtool.py\"),\n    \"attavo/claims.py\": (\"tests/test_claims.py\",),\n    \"attavo/clock.py\": (\"tests/test_clock.py\", \"tests/test_retry.py\"),\n    \"attavo/cli.py\": (\"tests/test_cli_help.py\", \"tests/test_testtool.py\"),\n    \"attavo/counsel.py\": (\"te